      "commands": [
        {
          "arguments": [],
          "commands": [],
          "description": "Creates a Batch and its optional first jobs, all or nothing. The answer is the Batch with each requested job in order, named by its \`id\` and \`customId\`, and whether it was created; read the job, or the job list, for how it stands. The hub checks the request shape first, a \`customId\` given twice included. A malformed job is refused before the agent's Output schema is checked, so a malformed job and an array Output schema take two attempts to diagnose. Once the shape is valid, the hub reports job input problems together with Output schemas that are invalid, describe a list or refer outside themselves. When the Output schema is invalid, the same 400 response includes any agent limits above the hub's maxima. A new Batch must meet the current limits. Retrying the same ID, agent, labels and breaker returns the existing Batch even after a maximum is lowered. Different Batch content under the same ID is refused with 422. Each custom ID follows the add's rule: matching content returns the held job even after cancellation, different content is refused with 422, and a cancelled Batch takes no new jobs (409).",
          "name": "create",
          "options": [
            {
              "attributeName": "id",
              "description": "The Batch's ID, unique in the Organization, which names it in every call; a UUID is made for it when left out. 1 to 100 letters, digits, \`_\` and \`-\`, not beginning with \`-\`, compared exactly, so \`Invoices\` and \`invoices\` are two Batches. Creating a Batch again with the same \`id\` and the same \`agent\`, \`labels\` and \`breaker\` returns the Batch already created, so a creation can be retried safely; with any of them different it is refused. A new Batch needs a new ID.; Min length: 1; Max length: 100; Pattern: ^[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_\\-]*$",
              "flags": "--id [string]",
              "name": "id",
              "negate": false,
              "optional": true,
              "required": false,
              "variadic": false,
