              "negate": false,
              "optional": false,
              "required": true,
              "variadic": false,
            },
            {
              "attributeName": "jobs",
              "description": "The jobs to add in this call. Each new job takes the timeout and model budget stored on the Batch at creation, even if the defaults or maxima at \`GET /jobs/limits\` have since changed. For a larger Batch, add more jobs with the same Batch ID in later calls.; Min items: 1; Max items: 1000 array",
              "flags": "--jobs [values...]",
              "name": "jobs",
              "negate": false,
              "optional": true,
              "required": false,
              "variadic": true,
            },
            {
              "attributeName": "labels",
              "defaultValue": {},
              "description": "Labels every job of the Batch gets, beside its own, which win where both name a key; none by default. Keys follow Kubernetes's label key syntax; values are any text of at most 256 characters, kept exactly as given. A job has at most 64 labels, the Batch's and its own together, so a job whose own labels take it past that is refused.; Property names: {"type":"string","pattern":"^(?:(?=.{1,253}\\\\/)[a-z0-9](?:[\\\\-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?(?:\\\\.[a-z0-9](?:[\\\\-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?)*\\\\/)?[A-Za-z0-9](?:[\\\\-_.A-Za-z0-9]{0,61}[A-Za-z0-9])?$"}; Max properties: 64",
