              "optional": true,
              "required": false,
              "variadic": false,
            },
            {
              "attributeName": "breaker",
              "defaultValue": true,
              "description": "The failure breaker, which pauses the Batch when a flaw its jobs share shows, after a few jobs instead of after all of them. The Batch's first \`canary\` jobs (5 by default), its Canary, run before the rest are released, and any of them failing pauses the Batch. Once every Canary place is filled and its jobs have ended, it pauses when more than \`maxFailurePercent\` (10 by default) of the jobs ended since the Canary began have failed. A job counts once, by its latest end; a job that a limit stopped counts as failed, while a cancelled job, or one its Runner's removal ended, does not count. Resuming a pause the breaker made starts a new Canary of the next \`canary\` jobs, those added later included. \`canary: 0\` releases every job at once, and the percentage then judges from the first job to end, so one early failure still pauses the Batch; \`maxFailurePercent: 100\` keeps the Canary alone. \`true\` by default, for the defaults; \`false\` turns the breaker off.; Any of: [{"type":"boolean"},{"type":"object","properties":{"canary":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":2147483647},"maxFailurePercent":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":100}},"additionalProperties":false}]",
