          "description": "Adds jobs to a Batch, at most 1000 at a time, each running the Batch's agent on its own \`input\` and files, and answers with the Batch and each job in the order given, named by its \`id\` and \`customId\`, with whether this add created it; read the job, or the job list, for how it stands. An add is all or nothing. The hub checks the request shape first, a \`customId\` given twice in the call included, and refuses a malformed add with 400 before it looks the Batch up; a well-formed add to a missing Batch is refused with 404. For an existing Batch, every job is then checked against it, and the add is refused with 400 if any is invalid, such as a job whose labels and the Batch's are too many together. The add is refused with 422 if the Batch already has a job with the same \`customId\` and different content, or with 409 if any job would be new and the Batch is cancelled. Each reported job problem names its path, such as \`jobs[17].input\`. On a successful add, a job the Batch still holds with the same \`customId\` and content is returned with \`created: false\`. Deleting a job frees its \`customId\`, so adding it again creates a new job with \`created: true\`. Jobs added to a paused Batch wait for it.",
